  "custom_origin_note": "workspace_policy.rs/tests adapt preceding project support at source base f507; auth_reload.rs/auth_acquisition.rs and their test files are project-private support introduced here. Upstream manager anchors are derivation/context for native adaptation, not claimed upstream declarations for these custom helpers.",
  "contracts": [
    {
      "name": "loaded result",
      "description": "LoadedAuth carries policy stamp and Replace(Some/None) versus Preserve(attempted/failure). AuthLoadError distinguishes Policy, Source and CacheUnavailable. Actual reload and guarded reload consume it through commit_auth_load."
    },
    {
      "name": "commit",
      "description": "Credentials write lock precedes exact policy guard. Prepare comparisons outside policy lock; only owned swaps inside it. Assignment is the policy linearization point. Drop policy guard before native network/watch notifications, retain credentials lock through notifications, and drop retired auth/failure values and trace after locks."
    },
    {
      "name": "origin",
      "description": "Native source/parsing and actual external resolver Transient errors preserve cache. Successful absence/native filtering and private NativePolicyRejection are authoritative None. External Restriction Transient clears; Permanent/Policy preserve existing classifier-specific disposition. Unknown permission errors stay Source."
    },
    {
      "name": "failure metadata",
      "description": "Install permanent failure metadata only for matching current credentials under a current policy guard. Preserve never restores attempted old auth over a newer cache."
    },
    {
      "name": "actual acquisition and legacy projections",
      "description": "Public reload bool retains coarse auth equality; guarded reload retains credential-change projection. Raw auth_cached stays unchecked. Every actual auth() return, including proactive-refresh error fallback, and the final auth_with_http_client_factory capture validate the CURRENT cache directly against native restrictions. Credential read lock prevents a concurrent cached replacement during validation/preparation; exact policy guard provides the acquisition linearization check. Only two fixed native preparation closures run before policy lock; prepared values are returned/dropped after guards. Unavailable/stale/rejected policy returns None without clearing newer cached credentials."
    }
  ],
